        "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/marshallpierce/rust-base64/issues/279",
        "number": 279,
        "state": "open",
        "locked": false,
        "title": "Clarify the docs of `NO_PAD`, add shorthands for indifferent decoding.",
        "user": {
          "login": "de-vri-es",
          "id": 786213,
          "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjc4NjIxMw==",
          "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/786213?v=4",
          "gravatar_id": "",
          "url": "https://api.github.com/users/de-vri-es",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/de-vri-es",
          "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/de-vri-es/followers",
          "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/de-vri-es/following{/other_user}",
          "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/de-vri-es/gists{/gist_id}",
          "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/de-vri-es/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
          "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/de-vri-es/subscriptions",
          "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/de-vri-es/orgs",
          "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/de-vri-es/repos",
          "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/de-vri-es/events{/privacy}",
          "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/de-vri-es/received_events",
          "type": "User",
          "user_view_type": "public",
          "site_admin": false
        },
        "body": "This PR tweaks the documentation of the `general_purpose::NO_PAD` configuration. The wording could be interpreted as \"does not require padding when decoding\" instead of \"requires that there is no padding when decoding\".\r\n\r\nThe PR also adds indifferent variants of the padding configs, mostly because in many applications, I think that is the most sane behaviour: be strict in what you generate, be lenient in what you accept.\r\n\r\nI didn't add any shorthands for the engines, as that would mean adding 4 new constants in total (`STANDARD_PAD_INDIFFERENT`, `STANDARD_NO_PAD_INDIFFERENT`, `URL_SAFE_PAD_INDIFFERENT` and `URL_SAFE_NO_PAD_INDIFFERENT`).\r\n\r\nPersonally, I would like to add those too, since I think `[NO_]PAD_INDIFFERENT` is most often the correct choice. However, I wanted to check here if adding those would be appreciated first.",
