        "closed_at": null,
        "author_association": "NONE",
        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "body": "I was wondering if there exists functionality in `cotengra` or `quimb` or `opt_einsum` to parse a file for the purposes of calculating contraction costs alone, without needing or caring about the elements contained within the tensors themselves.\r\n\r\nFor instance, `networkx` has a [`read_edgelist`](https://networkx.github.io/documentation/stable/reference/readwrite/generated/networkx.readwrite.edgelist.read_edgelist.html) function and `kahypar` has a way to parse files in the `hMetis` format to build hypergraphs. One or both of these could be used to construct tensor networks with arbitrary elements where the aim is to optimize contraction costs. \r\n\r\nIf something like this doesn't exist, I'd be interested in working on it. Please advise.",
