        "labels": [
          {
            "id": 1821824723,
            "node_id": "MDU6TGFiZWwxODIxODI0NzIz",
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/MouseLand/cellpose/labels/bug",
            "name": "bug",
            "color": "d73a4a",
            "default": true,
            "description": "Something isn't working"
          }
        ],
        "state": "open",
        "locked": false,
        "assignee": null,
        "assignees": [],
        "milestone": null,
        "comments": 0,
        "created_at": "2025-01-01T15:17:19Z",
        "updated_at": "2025-01-01T15:17:19Z",
        "closed_at": null,
        "author_association": "NONE",
        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "body": "**Describe the bug**\r\nSeveral sources indicate that there should be three outputs from `train_seg`, i.e., `model_path`, `train_losses` and `test_losses`:\r\n- The [definition](https://github.com/MouseLand/cellpose/blob/fc2949285451f0fe14456572c5eb09bc2e5fd642/cellpose/train.py#L373) for `cellpose.train.train_seg` describes the three outputs above. The [output](https://github.com/MouseLand/cellpose/blob/fc2949285451f0fe14456572c5eb09bc2e5fd642/cellpose/train.py#L549) from this function indicates the same.\r\n- If calling `cellpose` for training from the cmd line, the associated [code](https://github.com/MouseLand/cellpose/blob/537c65d329a61d770dcc5f192331a0b1f0a8ba0a/cellpose/__main__.py#L301) yields just the first element of the output. The GUI [code](https://github.com/MouseLand/cellpose/blob/537c65d329a61d770dcc5f192331a0b1f0a8ba0a/cellpose/gui/gui.py#L2182) is similar.\r\n- The test for `train_seg` obtains the path as the first element of the [output](https://github.com/MouseLand/cellpose/blob/v3.1.0/tests/test_train.py#L17).\r\n\r\nThat said, using Cellpose 3.1.0 to call `cellpose.train.train_seg` directly from the python cmd line with the three outputs specified yields the error:\r\n> Traceback (most recent call last):\r\n>   File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\r\n> TypeError: cannot unpack non-iterable PosixPath object\r\n\r\nCalling with just one output succeeds with path to the new model as the only output.\r\n\r\nThe API documentation for the [function](https://cellpose.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api.html#cellpose.train.train_seg) is ambiguous in that it says three outputs are returned but only describes the type for the path. The GitHub training documentation also [indicates](https://github.com/MouseLand/cellpose/blob/537c65d329a61d770dcc5f192331a0b1f0a8ba0a/docs/train.rst?plain=1#L78) that three outputs are possible.\r\n\r\nPlease tell me if there's something I'm missing.\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\nI am calling `cellpose.train.train_seg` from the python cmd line to retrain the `cyto3` Cellpose model:\r\n```\r\nmodel = cellpose.models.CellposeModel(gpu=True, model_type='cyto3', pretrained_model='cyto3')\r\nmodel_path, train_losses, test_losses = cellpose.train.train_seg(net=model.net,\r\n                         train_data=train_data,\r\n                         train_labels=train_labels,\r\n                         test_data=test_data,\r\n                         test_labels=test_labels,\r\n                         channels=channels,\r\n                         model_name=\"my_new_model\",\r\n                         save_path=\"./test_path/\",\r\n                         )\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Screenshots**\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6868d691-55e7-4e51-a981-ca88d4da2617)\r\n",
